IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg4-s204-ratification`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law (8 Del. C. ch. 1), section 205: proceedings regarding the validity of defective
-- corporate acts and stock. Layer 1, from the text alone. Quote lines are copied from de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt by script.
--
-- The Court of Chancery is an official: it has no seat. Its powers appear as what a person may ask it for and what
-- the corporation and the others affected are liable to (the Hohfeld correlative of a power is a liability), and a
-- judgment the Court makes is an input ("the Court has determined ...").
-- The defined terms of section 204(h) ("defective corporate act", "putative stock", "validation effective time" ...)
-- are used here as section 204(h) says: "As used in this section and in § 205 of this title only".

§ `s 205 Proceedings regarding validity of defective corporate acts and stock`

§§ `s 205(a) Who may apply, and what the Court may determine`

-- Seven kinds of applicant. A person may be more than one; any one is enough.
-- src:734 | (a) Subject to subsection (f) of this section, upon application by the corporation, any successor entity to the corporation, any member of the board of directors, any record or beneficial holder of valid stock or putative stock, any record or beneficial holder of valid or putative stock as of the time of a defective corporate act ratified pursuant to § 204 of this title, or any other person claiming to be substantially and adversely affected by a ratification pursuant to § 204 of this title, the Court of Chancery may:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(a) (src:734)
DECLARE `s 205(a) Applicant` HAS
    `the corporation`                                                                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `a successor entity to the corporation`                                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `a member of the board of directors`                                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `a record or beneficial holder of valid stock or putative stock`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `a record or beneficial holder of valid or putative stock as of the time of a defective corporate act ratified under s 204` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a person claiming to be substantially and adversely affected by a ratification under s 204`                                IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(a) (src:734)
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 205(a) Applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205(a) the person is among those who may apply to the Court of Chancery` applicant MEANS
        applicant's `the corporation`
    OR  applicant's `a successor entity to the corporation`
    OR  applicant's `a member of the board of directors`
    OR  applicant's `a record or beneficial holder of valid stock or putative stock`
    OR  applicant's `a record or beneficial holder of valid or putative stock as of the time of a defective corporate act ratified under s 204`
    OR  applicant's `a person claiming to be substantially and adversely affected by a ratification under s 204`

-- (a)(1) to (5). Upon an application by one of those persons the Court may determine the matters below. (1) and (2) are
-- about a ratification pursuant to s 204 (so they need one to have been made); (3) is about an act "not ratified or not
-- ratified effectively"; (4) and (5) need no ratification.
-- src:735 | (1) Determine the validity and effectiveness of any defective corporate act ratified pursuant to § 204 of this title;
-- src:736 | (2) Determine the validity and effectiveness of the ratification of any defective corporate act pursuant to § 204 of this title;
-- src:737 | (3) Determine the validity and effectiveness of any defective corporate act not ratified or not ratified effectively pursuant to § 204 of this title;
-- src:738 | (4) Determine the validity of any corporate act or transaction and any stock, rights or options to acquire stock; and
-- src:739 | (5) Modify or waive any of the procedures set forth in § 204 of this title to ratify a defective corporate act.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(a)(1) to (5) (src:735-739)
DECLARE `s 205(a) Matter the Court may determine` IS ONE OF
    `the validity and effectiveness of a defective corporate act ratified pursuant to s 204`
    `the validity and effectiveness of the ratification of a defective corporate act pursuant to s 204`
    `the validity and effectiveness of a defective corporate act not ratified or not ratified effectively pursuant to s 204`
    `the validity of any corporate act or transaction and any stock, rights or options to acquire stock`
    `whether to modify or waive any of the procedures in s 204 to ratify a defective corporate act`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(a)(1) to (5) (src:735-739)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 205(a) Matter the Court may determine`
      `a person among those who may apply has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ratification of the act was made pursuant to s 204` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that ratification was effective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205(a) the Court of Chancery may determine the matter on the application` matter `a person among those who may apply has applied` `a ratification of the act was made pursuant to s 204` `that ratification was effective` MEANS
        `a person among those who may apply has applied`
    AND CONSIDER matter
        WHEN `the validity and effectiveness of a defective corporate act ratified pursuant to s 204` THEN `a ratification of the act was made pursuant to s 204`
        WHEN `the validity and effectiveness of the ratification of a defective corporate act pursuant to s 204` THEN `a ratification of the act was made pursuant to s 204`
        WHEN `the validity and effectiveness of a defective corporate act not ratified or not ratified effectively pursuant to s 204` THEN
            (   (NOT `a ratification of the act was made pursuant to s 204`)
             OR (NOT `that ratification was effective`))
        WHEN `the validity of any corporate act or transaction and any stock, rights or options to acquire stock` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `whether to modify or waive any of the procedures in s 204 to ratify a defective corporate act` THEN TRUE

§§ `s 205(b) The orders the Court may make`

-- In connection with an action under this section the Court may make the orders below. The ten are a closed list
-- whose last item is a general power; each is available once an action under this section has been brought.
-- src:740 | (b) In connection with an action under this section, the Court of Chancery may:
-- src:741 | (1) Declare that a ratification in accordance with and pursuant to § 204 of this title is not effective or shall only be effective at a time or upon conditions established by the Court;
-- src:742 | (2) Validate and declare effective any defective corporate act or putative stock and impose conditions upon such validation by the Court;
-- src:743 | (3) Require measures to remedy or avoid harm to any person substantially and adversely affected by a ratification pursuant to § 204 of this title or from any order of the Court pursuant to this section, excluding any harm that would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated;
-- src:744 | (4) Order the Secretary of State to accept an instrument for filing with an effective time specified by the Court, which effective time may be prior or subsequent to the time of such order, provided that the filing date of such instrument shall be determined in accordance with § 103(c)(3) of this title;
-- src:745 | (5) Approve a stock ledger for the corporation that includes any stock ratified or validated in accordance with this section or with § 204 of this title;
-- src:746 | (6) Declare that shares of putative stock are shares of valid stock or require a corporation to issue and deliver shares of valid stock in place of any shares of putative stock;
-- src:747 | (7) Order that a meeting of holders of valid stock or putative stock be held and exercise the powers provided to the Court under § 227 of this title with respect to such a meeting;
-- src:748 | (8) Declare that a defective corporate act validated by the Court shall be effective as of the time of the defective corporate act or at such other time as the Court shall determine;
-- src:749 | (9) Declare that putative stock validated by the Court shall be deemed to be an identical share or fraction of a share of valid stock as of the time originally issued or purportedly issued or at such other time as the Court shall determine; and
-- src:750 | (10) Make such other orders regarding such matters as it deems proper under the circumstances.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(b)(1) to (10) (src:740-750)
DECLARE `s 205(b) Order the Court may make` IS ONE OF
    `a declaration that a ratification in accordance with s 204 is not effective or is effective only at a time or on conditions established by the Court`
    `validation and a declaration of effect of a defective corporate act or putative stock, with conditions imposed by the Court`
    `a requirement of measures to remedy or avoid harm to a person substantially and adversely affected by a ratification or by an order of the Court`
    `an order to the Secretary of State to accept an instrument for filing with an effective time specified by the Court`
    `approval of a stock ledger for the corporation that includes stock ratified or validated`
    `a declaration that shares of putative stock are shares of valid stock, or a requirement that the corporation issue and deliver shares of valid stock in their place`
    `an order that a meeting of holders of valid stock or putative stock be held, with the Court's powers under s 227`
    `a declaration that a defective corporate act validated by the Court is effective as of the time of the act or at another time the Court determines`
    `a declaration that putative stock validated by the Court is deemed an identical share or fraction of a share of valid stock as of the time originally issued or at another time the Court determines`
    `such other orders regarding these matters as the Court deems proper under the circumstances`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(b) (src:740)
GIVEN order IS A `s 205(b) Order the Court may make`
      `an action under this section has been brought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205(b) the Court of Chancery may make the order in connection with the action` order `an action under this section has been brought` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `a declaration that a ratification in accordance with s 204 is not effective or is effective only at a time or on conditions established by the Court` THEN `an action under this section has been brought`
    WHEN `validation and a declaration of effect of a defective corporate act or putative stock, with conditions imposed by the Court` THEN `an action under this section has been brought`
    WHEN `a requirement of measures to remedy or avoid harm to a person substantially and adversely affected by a ratification or by an order of the Court` THEN `an action under this section has been brought`
    WHEN `an order to the Secretary of State to accept an instrument for filing with an effective time specified by the Court` THEN `an action under this section has been brought`
    WHEN `approval of a stock ledger for the corporation that includes stock ratified or validated` THEN `an action under this section has been brought`
    WHEN `a declaration that shares of putative stock are shares of valid stock, or a requirement that the corporation issue and deliver shares of valid stock in their place` THEN `an action under this section has been brought`
    WHEN `an order that a meeting of holders of valid stock or putative stock be held, with the Court's powers under s 227` THEN `an action under this section has been brought`
    WHEN `a declaration that a defective corporate act validated by the Court is effective as of the time of the act or at another time the Court determines` THEN `an action under this section has been brought`
    WHEN `a declaration that putative stock validated by the Court is deemed an identical share or fraction of a share of valid stock as of the time originally issued or at another time the Court determines` THEN `an action under this section has been brought`
    WHEN `such other orders regarding these matters as the Court deems proper under the circumstances` THEN `an action under this section has been brought`

-- (b)(3): the measures are for harm to a person substantially and adversely affected by a ratification or by a Court
-- order, "excluding any harm that would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or
-- effectuated".
-- src:743 | (3) Require measures to remedy or avoid harm to any person substantially and adversely affected by a ratification pursuant to § 204 of this title or from any order of the Court pursuant to this section, excluding any harm that would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(b)(3) (src:743)
GIVEN `the person is substantially and adversely affected by a ratification under s 204 or by an order of the Court under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the harm would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205(b)(3) the harm is harm the Court may require measures to remedy or avoid` `the person is substantially and adversely affected by a ratification under s 204 or by an order of the Court under this section` `the harm would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated` MEANS
        `the person is substantially and adversely affected by a ratification under s 204 or by an order of the Court under this section`
    AND (NOT `the harm would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated`)

-- (b)(4): the instrument is filed with the effective time the Court specifies, which may be before or after the order;
-- its filing date is the date determined under s 103(c)(3) (out of range: s 103 (piece dg1)).
-- src:744 | (4) Order the Secretary of State to accept an instrument for filing with an effective time specified by the Court, which effective time may be prior or subsequent to the time of such order, provided that the filing date of such instrument shall be determined in accordance with § 103(c)(3) of this title;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(b)(4) (src:744)
GIVEN `the filing date of the instrument determined in accordance with s 103(c)(3)` IS A DATE -- out of range: s 103(c)(3) (piece dg1)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 205(b)(4) the filing date of the instrument the Court orders accepted for filing` `the filing date of the instrument determined in accordance with s 103(c)(3)` MEANS
    `the filing date of the instrument determined in accordance with s 103(c)(3)`

§§ `s 205(c) Service, joinder and notice`

-- src:751 | Service of the application under subsection (a) of this section upon the registered agent of the corporation shall be deemed to be service upon the corporation, and no other party need be joined in order for the Court of Chancery to adjudicate the matter. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(c) (src:751)
GIVEN `the application was served on the registered agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205(c) the corporation is deemed to have been served with the application` `the application was served on the registered agent of the corporation` MEANS
    `the application was served on the registered agent of the corporation`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(c) (src:751)
GIVEN `an application under subsection (a) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205(c) another party must be joined for the Court of Chancery to adjudicate the matter` `an application under subsection (a) has been made` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:751 | In an action filed by the corporation, the Court may require notice of the action be provided to other persons specified by the Court and permit such other persons to intervene in the action.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(c) (src:751)
GIVEN `the action was filed by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(c) the Court may require notice of the action to other persons and permit them to intervene` `the action was filed by the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the action was filed by the corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 205(d) What the Court may consider`

-- src:752 | (d) In connection with the resolution of matters pursuant to subsections (a) and (b) of this section, the Court of Chancery may consider the following:
-- src:753 | (1) Whether the defective corporate act was originally approved or effectuated with the belief that the approval or effectuation was in compliance with the provisions of this title, the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation;
-- src:754 | (2) Whether the corporation and board of directors has treated the defective corporate act as a valid act or transaction and whether any person has acted in reliance on the public record that such defective corporate act was valid;
-- src:755 | (3) Whether any person will be or was harmed by the ratification or validation of the defective corporate act, excluding any harm that would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated;
-- src:756 | (4) Whether any person will be harmed by the failure to ratify or validate the defective corporate act; and
-- src:757 | (5) Any other factors or considerations the Court deems just and equitable.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(d)(1) to (5) (src:752-757)
DECLARE `s 205(d) Factor the Court may consider` IS ONE OF
    `whether the defective corporate act was originally approved or effectuated with the belief that it complied with this title, the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws`
    `whether the corporation and its board of directors have treated the defective corporate act as valid, and whether any person has acted in reliance on the public record that it was valid`
    `whether any person will be or was harmed by the ratification or validation of the defective corporate act`
    `whether any person will be harmed by the failure to ratify or validate the defective corporate act`
    `any other factor the Court deems just and equitable`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(d) (src:752)
GIVEN factor IS A `s 205(d) Factor the Court may consider`
      `the Court is resolving matters under subsections (a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205(d) the Court of Chancery may consider the factor` factor `the Court is resolving matters under subsections (a) and (b)` MEANS
    CONSIDER factor
    WHEN `whether the defective corporate act was originally approved or effectuated with the belief that it complied with this title, the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` THEN `the Court is resolving matters under subsections (a) and (b)`
    WHEN `whether the corporation and its board of directors have treated the defective corporate act as valid, and whether any person has acted in reliance on the public record that it was valid` THEN `the Court is resolving matters under subsections (a) and (b)`
    WHEN `whether any person will be or was harmed by the ratification or validation of the defective corporate act` THEN `the Court is resolving matters under subsections (a) and (b)`
    WHEN `whether any person will be harmed by the failure to ratify or validate the defective corporate act` THEN `the Court is resolving matters under subsections (a) and (b)`
    WHEN `any other factor the Court deems just and equitable` THEN `the Court is resolving matters under subsections (a) and (b)`

-- (d)(3): the harm to consider excludes any harm that would have resulted if the act had been valid when approved or effectuated.
-- src:755 | (3) Whether any person will be or was harmed by the ratification or validation of the defective corporate act, excluding any harm that would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(d)(3) (src:755)
GIVEN `the person will be or was harmed by the ratification or validation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the harm would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205(d)(3) the harm is to be considered` `the person will be or was harmed by the ratification or validation` `the harm would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated` MEANS
        `the person will be or was harmed by the ratification or validation`
    AND (NOT `the harm would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated`)

§§ `s 205(e) Exclusive jurisdiction`

-- src:758 | (e) The Court of Chancery is hereby vested with exclusive jurisdiction to hear and determine all actions brought under this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(e) (src:758)
GIVEN `the action is brought in the Court of Chancery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205(e) the court has jurisdiction to hear and determine the action brought under this section` `the action is brought in the Court of Chancery` MEANS
    `the action is brought in the Court of Chancery`

§§ `s 205(f) The 120-day limit`

-- No action asserting (1) that a defective corporate act or putative stock ratified in accordance with s 204 is void or
-- voidable due to a failure of authorization identified in the resolution adopted under s 204(b), or (2) that the Court
-- should declare in its discretion that a ratification not be effective or be effective only on certain conditions, may be
-- brought after the expiration of 120 days from the later of the validation effective time and the time the notice, if any,
-- required by s 204(g) is given. The limit does not apply to an action asserting that a ratification was not accomplished in
-- accordance with s 204, nor to a person to whom notice under s 204(d) or (g) was required to be given but was not.
-- src:759 | (f) Notwithstanding any other provision of this section, no action asserting:
-- src:760 | (1) That a defective corporate act or putative stock ratified in accordance with § 204 of this title is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization identified in the resolution adopted in accordance with 204(b) of this title; or
-- src:761 | (2) That the Court of Chancery should declare in its discretion that a ratification in accordance with § 204 of this title not be effective or be effective only on certain conditions,
-- src:762 | may be brought after the expiration of 120 days from the later of the validation effective time and the time notice, if any, that is required to be given pursuant to § 204(g) of this title is given with respect to such ratification, except that this subsection shall not apply to an action asserting that a ratification was not accomplished in accordance with § 204 of this title or to any person to whom notice of the ratification was required to have been given pursuant to § 204(d) or (g) of this title, but to whom such notice was not given.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(f) (src:759-762)
DECLARE `s 205(f) Kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `a claim that a defective corporate act or putative stock ratified under s 204 is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization identified in the resolution adopted under s 204(b)`
    `a claim that the Court should declare in its discretion that a ratification under s 204 not be effective or be effective only on certain conditions`
    `a claim that a ratification was not accomplished in accordance with s 204`
    `a claim of any other kind`

-- The last day to bring such an action: 120 days after the later of the validation effective time and the time notice
-- under s 204(g) is given, if such notice is required. The 120th day counts (fork F-D). If notice is required and has not yet
-- been given, the period has not begun to run and there is no last day yet (NOTHING).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(f) (src:762)
GIVEN `the day of the validation effective time` IS A DATE
      `notice is required to be given under s 204(g)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day notice under s 204(g) was given` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 205(f) the last day to bring an action of the kinds the subsection limits` `the day of the validation effective time` `notice is required to be given under s 204(g)` `the day notice under s 204(g) was given` MEANS
    IF `notice is required to be given under s 204(g)`
    THEN CONSIDER `the day notice under s 204(g) was given`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST given THEN JUST (`the date` (`period in days` 120) `after` (`s 204(h)(6) the later of two days` `the day of the validation effective time` given))
    ELSE JUST (`the date` (`period in days` 120) `after` `the day of the validation effective time`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(f) (src:759-762)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 205(f) Kind of claim`
      `the person was required to be given notice under s 204(d) or (g) and was not given it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day to bring the action` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the action is brought` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205(f) the action is barred by this subsection` kind `the person was required to be given notice under s 204(d) or (g) and was not given it` `the last day to bring the action` `the day the action is brought` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a claim that a ratification was not accomplished in accordance with s 204` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a claim of any other kind` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the person was required to be given notice under s 204(d) or (g) and was not given it`
        THEN FALSE
        ELSE CONSIDER `the last day to bring the action`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST lastDay THEN `the day the action is brought` GREATER THAN lastDay

§§ `s 205(a) and (f) taken together: may this person bring this action now`

-- "Subject to subsection (f)": a person among those who may apply may do so unless (f) bars the action.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(a) (src:734); § 205(f) (src:759-762)
GIVEN `the person is among those who may apply to the Court of Chancery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is barred by this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205(a) the person may bring the action` `the person is among those who may apply to the Court of Chancery` `the action is barred by this subsection` MEANS
        `the person is among those who may apply to the Court of Chancery`
    AND (NOT `the action is barred by this subsection`)
